Bucketing:
Bucketing is performance optimization technique used to organize data into fixed number of buckets (files) based on column hash.
It helps joins and aggregations to reduce shuffle

Bucketing divides data into fixed number of buckets using hash function on columnn


What Is Partitioning?
Partitioning in Spark (Data Lake context) means:
Physically organizing data into folder structure based on column values.
hashtag#Example:
If partitioned by order_date, data stored like:
/orders/
 order_date=2026-02-01/
 order_date=2026-02-02/.


hashtag#Why Partition?
Main purpose:
Enable partition pruning
Reduce data scanned
Improve query performance
Lower storage I/O cost.

hashtag#ExampleScenario (Retail Domain)
Orders table:
1 Billion records
Analysts query mostly by date
Query:

SELECT * FROM orders WHERE order_date = '2026-02-01'

Without partitioning:
Full table scan.
With partitioning:
Only that folder read.
Huge performance gain.

hashtag#How to Write Partitioned Data in PySpark?
df.write \
 .mode("overwrite") \
 .partitionBy("order_date") \
 .parquet("s3://data-lake/silver/orders/")

hashtag#Partition Pruning (Very Important)
When you filter:
df.filter(col("order_date") == "2026-02-01")


hashtag#Spark:
Skips all other partitions
Reads only matching folder
Check using:
df.explain(True)

Look for:
PartitionFilters.

What Is Bucketing?
Bucketing is:
Distributing data into fixed number of buckets using hash function.
Unlike partitioning:
Does not create folder hierarchy
Creates fixed number of files

Why Bucketing?
Main use case:
Optimize joins
Avoid shuffle during joins.
Improve fact-to-fact join performance.


hashtag#How Bucketing Works
Example:
Bucket by customer_id into 8 buckets.
Spark:
Hash(customer_id) % 8
Writes into 8 fixed buckets

If two tables:
Bucketed by same key.
Same number of buckets.
Spark can skip shuffle join.

hashtag#ExampleBucketingCode:
df.write \
 .bucketBy(8, "customer_id") \
 .sortBy("customer_id") \
 .mode("overwrite") \
 .saveAsTable("bucketed_orders")



hashtag#End-to-End Example (Retail Optimization)
Step 1:
 Partition by order_date
Step 2:
 Repartition before write

df.repartition(200).write \
 .partitionBy("order_date") \
 .parquet("path")

Step 3:
 Use Delta OPTIMIZE later.
